      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The overall customer service was very good and streamlined from first contact to finish. I highly recommend the installing team as these guys were the first tradies who actually listened when I've told them to not silicone broken roof tiles during the installation (our roof is old and the tiles are really brittle) but to exchange these. They even went out and bought more tiles to exchange and when these run out, placed the silicon-ed ones into a convenient position for me to exchange the next day. The inverter is installed neatly to the wall. I would give more stars for the installation if I could.I can't judge if it's the best system on the market but I'm really happy with it. We have generated recently on a good sunny day 37kwh which I think is great. Really nice is the inverter display showing what is currently generated and what is being used / fed into the grit. I took a star of as I think the Wifi connection to the Sungrow server seems to happen randomly - might be only due to my limited IT skills. As well, I've adjusted the system time after daylight saving and although it was completed successfully the time changes back to the original setting after a few minutes. Both these points aren't a deal breaker but it's just not 5 Stars.I would definitely do it again.",
